course: dictionary
lesson: 6873
title: Overheat: too hot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overheat means to become too hot. It can describe a thing or a person: a phone can overheat, and so can you. Its other forms are overheats, overheated and overheating, so watch the ending to see when it happened.
explain: «The Christmas tree lights were next to the curtains, and they overheated.» The lights got too hot, which is what overheat means. The clues are the small fire and the smoke: heat that gets too high can be dangerous.
explain: Context also shows whether the word is about a body, a machine or an animal. «On a hot day you can start to overheat.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Too hot fits, so your meaning is right. Swap it in and check.
fact: Overheat means to become too hot, or to make something too hot.
fact: «Overheated» is the past tense: «The room is overheated» means it is too hot.
fact: You can overheat a phone, a charger, a laptop, an engine, a person or a pet.
fact: Never leave a dog in a hot car, because animals can overheat quickly.
fact: A fuse melts to stop the wires in the walls from overheating if too much electricity flows.
exercise: «The laptop was left under a blanket, and it began to overheat.» What does overheat mean here? | *Become too hot | Fall off the bed | Turn off the lights | Become very cold
exercise: Find and copy the past tense of overheat in: «The engine overheated on the long hill.» | *overheated | hill | engine | long
exercise: «Cages must be kept in the shade, because small animals can overheat in the sun.» Why? | Animals like the dark best | The sun makes the cage go out | *Small animals can get too hot and become ill quickly in the sun | Shade makes the cage heavier
test: «Plugging too many things into one socket can make it overheat.» What does overheat mean? | *Become too hot | Become too cold | Become too quiet
test: «Your body is like an engine: on a hot day you can lose more water than you take in and start to overheat.» What does overheat mean here? | Start to feel too cold | Start to feel sleepy | *Start to get too hot
exam: «A girl put her Christmas tree lights next to the curtains, and they overheated.» Why is this dangerous? | Lights only work when they are cold | *The lights could get too hot and start a fire | The curtains would turn into lights | The room would become cooler
